#. type: Title =
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.43.2.txt:2
#, no-wrap
msgid "Git 2.43.2 Release Notes"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.43.2.txt:9
msgid ""
"Relative to Git 2.43.1, this release has two important fixes to allow \"git "
"imap-send\" to be built with NO_CURL defined, and to restore the forced "
"flushing behaviour when GIT_FLUSH=1 is set.  It also contains other, "
"unexciting, fixes that have already been merged to the 'master' branch of "
"the development towards the next major release."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title -
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.43.2.txt:11
#, no-wrap
msgid "Fixes since Git 2.43.1"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.43.2.txt:14
msgid "Update to a new feature recently added, \"git show-ref --exists\"."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.43.2.txt:17
msgid ""
"Rename detection logic ignored the final line of a file if it is an "
"incomplete line."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.43.2.txt:20
msgid ""
"\"git diff --no-rename A B\" did not disable rename detection but did not "
"trigger an error from the command line parser."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.43.2.txt:23
msgid ""
"\"git diff --no-index file1 file2\" segfaulted while invoking the external "
"diff driver, which has been corrected."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.43.2.txt:26
msgid ""
"Rewrite //-comments to /* comments */ in files whose comments prevalently "
"use the latter."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.43.2.txt:29
msgid ""
"A failed \"git tag -s\" did not necessarily result in an error depending on "
"the crypto backend, which has been corrected."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.43.2.txt:32
msgid ""
"\"git stash\" sometimes was silent even when it failed due to unwritable "
"index file, which has been corrected."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.43.2.txt:36
msgid ""
"Recent conversion to allow more than 0/1 in GIT_FLUSH broke the mechanism by "
"flipping what yes/no means by mistake, which has been corrected."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.43.2.txt:37
msgid "Also contains documentation updates, code clean-ups and minor fixups."
msgstr ""
